# *Same Ratios, Ten Times the Data*

@body

{table-group="cosmos-chi-square"}
| Testcross Offspring | Expected (e) | Observed (o) | Deviation (o &#8722; e) | $(o-e)^2$ | $\frac{(o-e)^2}{e}$ |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| (A&#8722;B&#8722;) | 2250 | 2200 | | | |
| (aaB&#8722;) | 2250 | 2100 | | | |
| (A&#8722;bb) | 2250 | 2310 | | | |
| (aabb) | 2250 | 2390 | | | |
| | | | | *&chi;^2^ = Sum* | |

Under unlinked conditions we would expect the numbers to come closer to the 2250 number

