- *&#61539;2 = Sum*

- *21.42*

=== layout: section

# Summary

=== layout: one-panel

# Key takeaways

@body

- For two unlinked genes, a dihybrid testcross has an expected offspring ratio of 1:1:1:1.
- Chi-square compares observed and expected counts across the four offspring classes.
- Four classes give three degrees of freedom; compare the statistic with the critical value.
- The same proportional differences can provide stronger evidence against the null hypothesis with more offspring.

